# Third-party component carried in this repository

## ephemora-cell 2.2.0 — Apache License 2.0

The WASM sandbox that executes a delivery and signs the execution report. Copyright Michael Soppa.
Redistributed here as an unmodified wheel so a judge can run the receipt path without network access
to a package index (the project is not published on PyPI).

- `ephemora_cell-2.2.0-py3-none-any.whl` — built from the Apache-2.0 source, no changes
  SHA-256 `178088f126af088f6ffaa56416340ede85940729b62a5b46423fa7a74e612a62`
- `LICENSE.ephemora-cell` — the licence text as shipped with the source
- `README.ephemora-cell.md` — the project's own readme, kept byte-for-byte from upstream so the
  documented behaviour matches the shipped wheel. Its relative links (`docs/…`, `benchmarks/…`)
  resolve in the upstream repository, not here — only this NOTICE file and the wheel are ours.

Source: `https://github.com/MichaelS1011/ephemora-cell`, version 2.2.0 — both read from the wheel's
own `METADATA`, not from a guess. Retrieved 2026-11-06 (see the phase-5 rows in docs/EVIDENCE_LOG.md).

Install together with its one runtime dependency:

    pip install wasmtime vendor/ephemora_cell-2.2.0-py3-none-any.whl

Verify before installing (no network needed):

    shasum -a 256 vendor/ephemora_cell-2.2.0-py3-none-any.whl
